// Ordered Fraymakers character-template animations + their AnimationStats.hx
// property overrides. Order & grouping match the official character-template.
// ONLY WHAT OUR OWN CONVERSION WIRES. A stock character's AnimationStats is that character's
// TUNING, and the engine merges a character's entry over its own defaults per field -- so every
// value here that the source did not state overrode the engine's answer with somebody else's.
// `aerial_down` was handed `allowMovement: false` and `special_down` `xSpeedConservation: 0`,
// which is why a down air could not drift and the tornado had no left/right to it, on all 44
// converted characters at once.
//
// What stays is structural: which animation a move LANDS into (a split this converter made), how
// it links to its own air/ground twin, how it ends, what state follows. How a move FEELS comes
// from the source, through the `updateAnimationStats` calls its own code makes, or from the
// engine's default when the source says nothing.
// A ground attack that leaves the floor stays in its state (leaveGroundType NONE) and keeps
// playing when it comes back down (landType NONE): the source runs an attack clip to its end
// either way, so a hop inside one is not a landing.
// Emitted by haxe_gen::generate_animation_stats; `props` is the object-literal body (empty = `{}`).
[
